abstract: |
  Biological Qubits and Quantum Sensors Atlas v4.0.0 is a consolidated,
  machine-readable catalogue of quantum systems operating in or compatible
  with biological environments (in vitro, in cellulo, in vivo), together
  with a curated collection of fluorescent-protein biosensors. Version
  4.0.0 is a clean re-release of the v3.0.0 scientific content on a pruned
  repository (the earlier v3.0.0 Zenodo bundle has been restricted because
  it shipped historical artefacts and binary files with embedded author
  metadata). The release introduces class A' (A-prime), a new category of
  fluorescent proteins demonstrating direct ODMR readout (EYFP, MagLOV,
  MagLOV2, mScarlet-FMN, mCherry-FMN, mScarlet-I-FMN, DmCry), and refreshes
  classes B, C and D with 2024 to 2026 literature (SiC alkene defects,
  BNNT, SnV/GeV nanodiamonds, hBN color centres, first-in-human HP
  13C,15N2-urea MRI, room-temperature FMO coherence, Flavin-Guanine
  SCRP, updated cryptochrome evidence). The fluorescent-biosensor atlas
  is extended with 2023 to 2026 biosensors (CaBLAM, HaloDA1.0, iGluSnFR4,
  ASAP4.4-Kv, PinkyCaMP, OCaMP, FR-GECO1a/1c, NEMOf/c, LifeCamp,
  ASAP6.1/6b, GRAB-NE2h). The dataset totals 82 qubits and 195 FP
  biosensors, with full provenance (DOI, PMCID, license) for every
  curated entry.
